And, you know, falling meteors are more common than you might think.

00:53:11.280 --> 00:53:19.200
Every day, the Earth is bombarded with thousands of pieces of rock that come from outer space.

00:53:18.320 --> 00:53:24.560
Now, as they enter the atmosphere, a tremendous friction is generated and they burst into flames.

00:53:23.880 --> 00:53:27.720
But if they survive that re-entry, then they become meteorites.

00:53:26.880 --> 00:53:31.280
Irregularly shaped, really heavy pieces of rock.

00:53:30.920 --> 00:53:38.200
But these space balls clearly weren't made of stone.

00:53:38.560 --> 00:53:48.520
So if they weren't meteorites, what were these alien orbs?

00:53:48.640 --> 00:53:54.880
At first, the scientist tasked with analysing the space balls was absolutely flummoxed.

00:53:56.360 --> 00:53:57.760
What a strange artefact.

00:53:56.920 --> 00:53:58.320
What a strange object.

00:53:58.360 --> 00:54:06.240
I've never seen anything similar before.

00:54:05.400 --> 00:54:12.560
Juan Antonio tested every bit of the ball.

00:54:16.120 --> 00:54:18.240
We found out the cover of the balls was made of carbon fibre.

00:54:17.840 --> 00:54:36.880
We discovered that some parts of the balls were made of a special stainless steel, and the metal of the main body was made of titanium.

00:54:36.080 --> 00:54:39.280
Right, so let's just get this straight.

00:54:38.440 --> 00:54:44.440
Fireballs, made of carbon fibre and titanium, are battering us from beyond our planet?

00:54:43.480 --> 00:54:47.640
So are these cannonballs a sign of intelligent life?

00:54:46.720 --> 00:54:48.080
Well, yes.

00:54:59.000 --> 00:55:04.800
You see, they are from outer space, but we put them there.

00:55:04.040 --> 00:55:10.640
These balls are fuel tanks, yes.

00:55:09.760 --> 00:55:13.160
Fuel tanks for powering rockets.

00:55:13.520 --> 00:55:17.200
'One small step for man.

00:55:16.280 --> 00:55:19.080
'One giant leap for mankind.'

00:55:18.320 --> 00:55:28.840
Since we began exploring space in the 1960s, nearly 7,000 satellites have been sent into orbit.

00:55:28.040 --> 00:55:37.800
And the metal balls found in Calasparra, Vietnam and Brazil are the remains of the small fuel tanks that are used to manoeuvre them.

00:55:37.120 --> 00:55:46.160
So, if they're supposed to be up in space, how did these fuel tanks end up in Spain?

00:55:46.200 --> 00:55:56.760
Well, sometimes satellites may break down or collide and the debris can fall back to Earth, or de-orbit.

00:55:55.920 --> 00:56:03.600
In a given month, 10 or 20 objects will de-orbit, that means they'll burn up in the atmosphere.

00:56:02.880 --> 00:56:09.760
When we have control over a de-orbit, we nearly always aim for the middle of the Pacific Ocean because it's a very big, uninhabited area.

00:56:08.840 --> 00:56:16.320
The problem is, when certain larger bits of debris de-orbit, larger pieces, fuel tanks etc, we have no control over where they'll land.

00:56:15.480 --> 00:56:21.840
We really won't know until very late in the de-orbit process.

00:56:22.840 --> 00:56:33.840
Whilst most debris burns up, robust parts like fuel tanks may survive re-entry.

00:56:32.880 --> 00:56:34.800
Realistically, space junk poses little risk of injury.

00:56:34.120 --> 00:56:37.480
It's much more dangerous hurtling around our planet.

00:56:36.600 --> 00:56:48.440
A paint fleck will have the same kinetic energy as a rifle bullet, and poses a real danger to spacecraft and asteroids.

00:56:47.560 --> 00:56:51.600
There are now millions of bits of debris circling the Earth.

00:56:50.720 --> 00:56:53.880
Some as big as a bus.

00:56:53.000 --> 00:56:57.840
And any collisions with the satellites we rely upon could jeopardise our whole way of life.

00:56:57.000 --> 00:57:07.480
The internet may go down because we rely on space-based communications more than ever in our connected society.

00:57:06.560 --> 00:57:11.520
A lot of the banking industry and finance industry relies on very accurate timing for high-frequency trading.

00:57:10.680 --> 00:57:16.400
If we lost those timing signals, there could be financial chaos.

00:57:15.640 --> 00:57:18.600
But don't worry, a global meltdown is highly unlikely.

00:57:17.760 --> 00:57:25.600
Space debris is very carefully monitored so that satellites can be moved out of harm's way.

00:57:24.800 --> 00:57:30.840
So, those strange Spanish balls weren't a sign of an alien attack.

00:57:30.000 --> 00:57:36.080
They were a symbol of the ever-increasing mass of space junk that's circling our planet.

00:57:38.680 --> 00:57:51.600
So, while Spain fell under attack by balls from space... ..an equally strange sphere was found underwater... ..and a mythical moss was uncovered underground.

00:57:53.440 --> 00:57:54.720
So there.

